.TH S2 1 "October 2026" "s2 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s2 \- Super Screenshot, a native X11 screenshot annotation editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s2
.RI [ input_path ]
.RB [ \-i " path|\-" ]
.RB [ \-o " path" ]
.RB [ \-C " class" ]
.RB [ \-D " absdir" ]
.RB [ \-\-modal ]
.RB [ \-c ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
s2 edits an existing capture with arrows, lines, shapes, text, numbered pins,
freehand strokes, highlights, blur and pixelation. Its view and floating controls
are excluded from exported PNGs. Fonts, icons and cursors are embedded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " path|\-"
Read an input image from a file or standard input. A positional path is equivalent.
.TP
.BI \-o " path"
Use this explicit output path when saving. Existing files may be overwritten.
Without this option, save to a unique timestamped PNG in the configured directory.
.TP
.BI \-D " absdir"
Override the timestamped save directory. Must be an absolute path.
.TP
.BI \-C " class"
Override both instance and class in X11 WM_CLASS.
.TP
.B \-\-modal
Request a centered floating dialog using X11 dialog/modal hints.
Placement is ultimately controlled by the window manager.
.TP
.B \-\-normal-window
Compatibility alias for the default regular, resizable and tileable window.
.TP
.B \-c
Copy the result when finishing successfully. Cancellation does not copy.
.TP
.B \-\-licenses
Print the embedded font license and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage.
.TP
.B \-v
Show version.
.SH FINISHING
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Commit pending input, save and exit. Honor an explicit \-o path; otherwise create
YYYY-MM-DDTHHMMSS.ffffff.png. Timestamp collisions receive numeric suffixes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Commit pending input, copy the PNG to the clipboard and exit.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Y
Copy the PNG and keep editing.
.TP
.B Enter
Finish text entry or custom hex input. Never saves the image.
.TP
.B Esc
In a regular window, cancel interactions and deselect. In modal mode, dismiss
transient UI/input first; otherwise cancel and quit. About always dismisses first.
.TP
.B q, WM Quit
Cancel and close. The app supports WM_DELETE_WINDOW for graceful WM Quit.
.SH TOOLS
s selects; a draws arrows; l lines; p pen; r rectangles; o circles; t text;
n numbered pins; h highlight regions; m marker strokes; b blur; x pixelation;
c samples a color. Text styling shortcuts take precedence while text is selected.
.PP
Drag to draw, or use Space to set/commit anchors. New annotations become selected.
Reselecting Number resets numbering to 1 without changing its size.
.SH SELECTION
Drag selected objects to move; drag empty canvas for marquee selection.
Delete/Backspace removes selected objects. Square handles resize; the round handle
rotates. Shift preserves aspect ratio or snaps rotation to 45 degrees.
Comma/period rotate by 15 degrees.
.PP
Drag a line/arrow midpoint diamond to curve; Shift-drag straightens.
On selected arrows e/E cycle end styles forward/backward; < and > toggle the
start/end. For other rotatable selections < and > rotate by 1 degree.
.SH APPEARANCE
[ and ] adjust the active tool or selected object dimension. Rectangle/circle
outlines use 3-pixel steps; text/pins 8 pixels; marker width 8 pixels; blur 3 pixels;
highlight strength 5 percentage points. Other strokes/pixelate blocks use 1 pixel.
.PP
1 through 9 choose foreground/stroke colors. Shift+numbers choose rectangle,
circle or text fill colors. The color menu includes Stroke/Text and Fill targets,
custom hex entry and image sampling. Shift-click opens Fill directly.
.PP
f toggles fill. Shift+F independently toggles rectangle/circle outlines.
g toggles gradient fills, including text backgrounds, pins, highlights and filled
arrow ends. Changes apply to compatible selected objects and future defaults.
.SH TEXT
Enter commits and selects text; t edits selected text in place. Left/Right,
Home/End, Shift selection, Ctrl+A, Backspace/Delete and Ctrl+V are supported.
Esc cancels editing. The editor is single-line and uses keyboard caret placement.
.PP
For selected text: b/B decreases/increases weight; i toggles italic;
u underline; s strikethrough; p/P padding; c/C corner radius; [/] font size.
.SH VIEW AND THEMES
+ zooms in; \- zooms out; = fits (0 is an alias).
Ctrl+wheel zooms around the pointer; Ctrl+left-drag pans.
Fit resets panning. Exports retain original capture dimensions.
.PP
Click the theme name, Alt+C, or Alt-click the color control for the theme menu.
Alt+1 through Alt+9 select presets. Theme mappings/modifier are configurable.
? opens keyboard help. The adjacent info button opens About with a clickable
repository link, license, author and version. Tab/Enter navigate About.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit config.h and rebuild. It is copied from config.def.h only when missing.
Settings include palette, tool dimensions, save directory, typography,
S2_DEFAULT_GRADIENT_FILL, S2_DEFAULT_SHAPE_OUTLINE, S2_ARROW_EDGE_CYCLE,
S2_DEFAULT_ARROW_EDGE_STYLE, S2_THEME_PRESETS and S2_THEME_MODIFIER.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates successful save, copy or cancellation. Errors return nonzero.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
X11, Cairo, Pango, HarfBuzz, Fontconfig, FreeType/Xft and libpng.
xclip handles clipboard operations; xdg-open opens repository links.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
maim -s | s2 --modal -i -
s2 capture.png -o annotated.png
s2 capture.png -D /tmp
.fi
